.TH geectl-request-change-review-state 1  "geectl-request-change-review-state 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-change\-review\-state \- Change the state of one review on a submit request: accept it, decline it, or reopen it to new
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request change\-review\-state\fR [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-comment\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> <\fISTATE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the state of one review on a submit request: accept it, decline it, or reopen it to new
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
The user the review was asked of
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
The group the review was asked of
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The project the review was asked of
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
The package the review was asked of (needs its project)
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR [default: ]
The message left with the change. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a comment may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The request id
.TP
<\fISTATE\fR>
The state to change the review to
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
new
.IP \(bu 2
accepted
.IP \(bu 2
declined
.RE
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
